## 6. UI — Shell (`lge_imgui.h`)

**Lucid namespace:** N/A — engine-internal C++ only

ImGui is the engine shell's UI backend. It is not exposed to Lucid code or game extensions — shell panels (inspector, hierarchy, console, asset browser) are written in C++ by the engine team. This header is not included in `lge_api.h` and is invisible to `LGE_GetAPI()` callers.

### Functions

```cpp
// Called once at boot after RHI is ready.
void ImGuiShell_Init(void* vulkan_swapchain);

// Called at start of each frame, before any panel code runs.
void ImGuiShell_BeginFrame();

// Called after all panel code, before RHI_EndFrame.
// Flushes all ImGui draw calls into the RHI command buffer.
void ImGuiShell_EndFrame();

// Shutdown — frees ImGui font atlas and GPU resources.
void ImGuiShell_Shutdown();
```

### Style Constants (set once in `editor_theme.cpp`)

```cpp
// Applied globally at boot via ImGui::GetStyle() and ImGui::GetIO()
// Colors
ImGuiStyle.Colors[ImGuiCol_WindowBg]   = ImVec4(0.12, 0.12, 0.12, 1.0);
ImGuiStyle.Colors[ImGuiCol_FrameBg]    = ImVec4(0.18, 0.18, 0.18, 1.0);
ImGuiStyle.Colors[ImGuiCol_Button]     = ImVec4(0.22, 0.22, 0.22, 1.0);
ImGuiStyle.Colors[ImGuiCol_Border]     = ImVec4(0.30, 0.30, 0.30, 1.0);
// Rounding
ImGuiStyle.WindowRounding  = 6.0f;
ImGuiStyle.FrameRounding   = 4.0f;
ImGuiStyle.GrabRounding    = 4.0f;
// Borders
ImGuiStyle.WindowBorderSize = 1.0f;
ImGuiStyle.FrameBorderSize  = 0.0f;
```

### Notes
- Any engine developer adding a new shell panel writes a C++ function that calls standard ImGui widgets (`ImGui::Text`, `ImGui::Button`, `ImGui::InputFloat`, etc.) between `BeginFrame` and `EndFrame`.
- Alpha transparency is set per-window via `ImGui::SetNextWindowBgAlpha()` or globally via `ImGuiCol_WindowBg`'s alpha channel — no extra render pass needed.
- For PNG icons and thumbnails: load via `stb_image`, upload with `LGE_UploadTexture()`, pass the `TextureID` cast to `ImTextureID` to `ImGui::Image()`.

