## 7. UI — In-Game (`lge_ui.h`)

**Lucid namespace:** `api.ui`

RmlUI backend for in-game HUDs, menus, and UI attached to world entities via `UIComponent`. Game developers interact with this through the Lucid UI Bridge (the `ui:` call syntax) rather than raw function calls. The bridge translates Lucid's declarative `ui:div`, `ui:button` etc. into calls below.

### Types

```cpp
using RmlContextID = uint32_t;   // one context per UIComponent / per screen document
using ElementID    = uint32_t;   // handle to a specific element inside a context

#define LGE_INVALID_CONTEXT ((RmlContextID)0)
```

### Functions

```cpp
// --- Context lifecycle ---

// Create a new RmlUI context at the given resolution.
// width/height — pixel dimensions; can differ from screen size (world-space UI)
// Returns LGE_INVALID_CONTEXT on failure.
RmlContextID LGE_UI_CreateContext(uint32_t width, uint32_t height);

// Destroy a context and all its documents/elements.
void LGE_UI_DestroyContext(RmlContextID ctx);

// --- Document management ---

// Load an .rml file into a context. The document is shown immediately.
// Returns false if the file cannot be found in the VFS.
bool LGE_UI_LoadDocument(RmlContextID ctx, const char* rml_path);

// Unload all documents from a context (clears the screen).
void LGE_UI_ClearDocuments(RmlContextID ctx);

// --- Element property binding (the Reactive Bridge) ---

// Set a CSS property on a named element (e.g. "color", "width", "display").
// Changes only the named property — does not trigger a full re-layout.
void LGE_UI_SetProperty(
    RmlContextID ctx,
    const char*  element_id,
    const char*  property,
    const char*  value       // CSS value string: "red", "100px", "none", etc.
);

// Set the inner text of a named element.
void LGE_UI_SetText(RmlContextID ctx, const char* element_id, const char* text);

// Show or hide an element without removing it from the DOM.
void LGE_UI_SetVisible(RmlContextID ctx, const char* element_id, bool visible);

// --- Events ---

// Register a click callback for a named element.
void LGE_UI_OnClick(
    RmlContextID ctx,
    const char*  element_id,
    void (*callback)(const char* element_id)
);

// --- Per-frame update (called by UISystem for each active UIComponent) ---

// Pump RmlUI's internal event queue and submit draw calls to the RHI.
void LGE_UI_UpdateAndRender(RmlContextID ctx);
```

### Lucid-side (`api.ui` / `ui:` bridge)

```lucid
-- Declarative UI (the normal way — Lucid UI Bridge)
export const on_render_hud (ui &Ui) = {
    ui:div("hud-root", () = {
        ui:progress_bar("health-bar", &this.health)
        ui:text("ammo-counter", string(this.ammo) + " / " + string(this.max_ammo))

        ui:div("buff-list", () = {
            for buff in this.active_buffs {
                ui:icon("buff-icon", buff.icon_path)
            }
        })
    })
}

-- Direct property binding (reactive — updates only the changed property)
ui:progress_bar("health-bar", &health)   -- binds health variable; updates on change

-- Register activity bar panel (editor extension)
api.ui:register_activity_bar("My Tool", "resources/icon.svg", open_panel)

-- Register a file icon for a custom file type
api.ui:register_file_icon(".lanim", "resources/anim_icon.svg")

-- Create a raw Vulkan canvas for custom drawing
let canvas &Canvas = api.ui:create_canvas(tab)
```

### Notes
- `LGE_UI_SetProperty` and `LGE_UI_SetText` are the primary update calls — they mutate in place without rebuilding the DOM tree. Avoid calling `LGE_UI_LoadDocument` every frame; load once, update via property bindings.
- Each `UIComponent` entity owns exactly one `RmlContextID`. The `UISystem` iterates all active `UIComponent` entities and calls `LGE_UI_UpdateAndRender` on each every frame.
- `.rcss` stylesheets are loaded automatically when an `.rml` document references them. They can also be injected at runtime for theming via `LGE_UI_InjectStylesheet()` (see extended API).

