## 11. Extension System (`lge_ext.h`)

**Lucid namespace:** `api.ext` (engine and editor facing)

Loads and manages extensions — separately distributed `.dll` / `.lmod` packages that register new components, systems, commands, or UI panels. Extensions declare their requirements in an `extension.json` manifest.

### Types

```cpp
using ExtensionID = uint32_t;
#define LGE_INVALID_EXTENSION ((ExtensionID)0)
```

### Functions

```cpp
// Load an extension from a directory (must contain extension.json + the module).
// Reads extension.json, verifies the Ed25519 signature, version-checks against the
// kernel, then calls on_load(api) on the module.
// Returns LGE_INVALID_EXTENSION on any failure.
ExtensionID LGE_Ext_Load(const char* extension_dir);

// Unload an extension. Calls on_unload(), unregisters all commands/components
// registered by this extension, then frees the library.
void LGE_Ext_Unload(ExtensionID id);

// Returns true if an extension with the given ID string is currently loaded.
// id_string — the "id" field from extension.json (e.g. "com.studio.my-tool")
bool LGE_Ext_IsLoaded(const char* id_string);

// Iterate all currently loaded extensions.
void LGE_Ext_ForEach(void (*callback)(ExtensionID id, const char* name, const char* version));
