### The `extension.json` Manifest

```json
{
  "id":           "com.studio.animation-tools",
  "name":         "Animation Tools",
  "version":      "1.2.0",
  "api_version":  "1.0.0",
  "entry_point":  "animation_tools.lmod",
  "permissions":  ["fs.read", "fs.write", "ecs.register", "ui.panel"],
  "signature":    "<Ed25519 signature of the bundle contents>"
}
```

### Lucid-side (extension `on_load` hook)

```lucid
-- Every extension entry point receives the api object at load time
on_load (api) = {
    -- Register a menu item and a command
    api.menu:register("View/Animation Tools", open_anim_panel)
    api.commands:register("animation.open", open_anim_panel)

    -- Register an activity bar panel
    api.ui:register_activity_bar("Animation", "resources/anim_icon.svg", open_anim_panel)

    -- Register a custom file icon
    api.ui:register_file_icon(".lanim", "resources/anim_file_icon.svg")
}

on_unload = {
    -- Clean up any persistent state here
}
```

### Notes
- Extensions are loaded from `extensions/` inside the active project, plus a global `engine_extensions/` directory.
- The kernel verifies the `extension.json` Ed25519 signature against the trusted publisher list before loading. Unsigned extensions are rejected in production builds.
- Permissions declared in `extension.json` are enforced at the ABI level — calling `LGE_VFS_Write` from an extension without `"fs.write"` permission returns false and logs a warning.

