## 16. Platform (`lge_platform.h`)

**Lucid namespace:** N/A — engine-internal only. Not exposed to extensions.

Isolates all OS-specific code. The rest of the kernel only calls these functions — it never calls `LoadLibrary`, `dlopen`, `ReadDirectoryChangesW`, or `inotify` directly.

### Functions

```cpp
using ModuleHandle = void*;
using ThreadHandle = void*;

// --- Window ---
void  Platform_Init(const char* title, uint32_t w, uint32_t h);
void  Platform_PollEvents();      // pump OS message queue; called once per frame
void* Platform_GetNativeWindow(); // HWND on Windows, Window on X11/Wayland
bool  Platform_ShouldClose();     // true when the user clicks X or calls Shutdown

// --- Dynamic library loading ---
ModuleHandle Platform_LoadModule(const char* path);
void*        Platform_GetSymbol(ModuleHandle mod, const char* symbol_name);
void         Platform_UnloadModule(ModuleHandle mod);

// --- Threading ---
ThreadHandle Platform_SpawnThread(void (*fn)(void*), void* user_data);
void         Platform_JoinThread(ThreadHandle t);
void         Platform_DetachThread(ThreadHandle t); // fire and forget

// --- File watching (used by Script Manager for hot-reload) ---
using FileChangedCallback = void (*)(const char* path);
void  Platform_WatchDir(const char* dir_path, FileChangedCallback on_change);
void  Platform_StopWatch(const char* dir_path);
```

### Notes
- On Windows: `Platform_LoadModule` wraps `LoadLibraryA`, `Platform_GetSymbol` wraps `GetProcAddress`, and `Platform_WatchDir` wraps `ReadDirectoryChangesW`.
- On Linux: `Platform_LoadModule` wraps `dlopen`, `Platform_GetSymbol` wraps `dlsym`, and `Platform_WatchDir` wraps `inotify_add_watch`.
- Adding a new platform (e.g. console) means implementing this file only — no other kernel files change.

